ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69814029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid","html_url":"https://github.com/DissonantVoid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DissonantVoid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-12T23:59:03Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T23:59:03Z","body":"@VojtaStruhar can you please elaborate? Using `NodePath` was my first thought but it doesn't seem to work either, I can't tell if it's part of the bug.\n\nHere's a minimal project where the `NodePath` approach doesn't work:\n\n[export_storage_bug_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20717558/export_storage_bug_test.zip)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2968479280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2969236419","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102621#issuecomment-2969236419","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102621","id":2969236419,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6w-vPD","user":{"login":"VojtaStruhar","id":49688205,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5Njg4MjA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49688205?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar","html_url":"https://github.com/VojtaStruhar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T06:37:20Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T06:37:20Z","body":"@DissonantVoid your mrp project contains a mistake. In `test.gd` on line 10\n\n```gdscript\n_node_path = node.get_path()  # Wrong, don't use absolute paths\n_node_path = self.get_path_to(node)  # CORRECT - relative path\n```\n\nYour code does what it's told! You want to use a relative path in the [`get_node`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_node.html#class-node-method-get-node) function you are using on line 19. When you create an absolute path to a node within the editor, it contains all the UI parent nodes of the Godot editor! That means it will surely break on the start of the game.\n\nUse relative paths!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2969236419/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]